    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60-a10">

                <pb facs="0123" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg43"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ragsdale to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your dispatches of November 30, and to report that I have complied with the
                    instructions therein required. I also inclose copies of the protest sent by me
                    to the consul-general of France and the consul of Russia.</p>
                <pb facs="0124" n="44" xml:id="pg44"/>
                <p>In this connection I desire to say that I have not yet been able to procure an
                    intelligent map of the concessions proposed, although they were promised to me.
                    I will make another effort.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James W. Ragsdale</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
